{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}{{ 'control_plane.title'|trans }}{% endblock %}

{#
	The same empty page as a tenant's sign-in (XIV-79): one centred card, and none
	of the frame that belongs to an application the reader has not been admitted
	to. The version still shows, inside the card, for the reason it shows there —
	it is the first question about any bug report and this is the page "I cannot
	sign in" is written from.
#}
{% block footer %}{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
	<main class="signin-shell">
		<div class="card shadow-sm" style="width: 22rem;">
			<div class="card-body p-4 text-center">
				{#
					**No tenant mark here, and that is not an omission** (XIV-49,
					XIV-57). A customer's sign-in page draws the customer's own logo
					because the installation should read as their product; this page
					is not any customer's, and there is no tenant resolved on this
					host to have one — the control-plane hostname is a system host
					precisely so that nothing here can be about one customer.

					`_brand_mark.html.twig` would fall through to Xivi's own mark,
					which a deployment supplies and a clean checkout has not got, so
					including it would draw nothing most of the time and something
					indistinguishable from the tenant page the rest of it. The
					heading says what this is instead, in words, which is the one
					thing a reader standing here needs to know.
				#}
				<h1 class="h5 mb-1">{{ 'control_plane.title'|trans }}</h1>
				{#
					Which installation's control plane, under the name of the thing
					itself. The hostname rather than a label somebody configured: on
					a page with one card and no navigation it is the only line that
					distinguishes this deployment from another, and it is the line a
					stale bookmark gets wrong.
				#}
				<p class="text-body-secondary small mb-4">{{ app.request.host }}</p>

				{% if error %}
					{# Symfony's own `security` domain again (XIV-8): "Invalid
					   credentials." is the framework's sentence, not ours. #}
					<div class="alert alert-danger py-2 small" role="alert">
						{{ error.messageKey|trans(error.messageData, 'security') }}
					</div>
				{% endif %}

				<form method="post" action="{{ path('control_plane_login') }}">
					<div class="mb-3 text-start">
						<label for="email" class="form-label">{{ 'common.email'|trans }}</label>
						<input type="email" id="email" name="email" value="{{ last_email }}"
						       class="form-control" autocomplete="username" required autofocus>
					</div>

					<div class="mb-4 text-start">
						<label for="password" class="form-label">{{ 'common.password'|trans }}</label>
						<input type="password" id="password" name="password"
						       class="form-control" autocomplete="current-password" required>
					</div>

					<input type="hidden" name="_csrf_token" value="{{ csrf_token('authenticate') }}">

					<button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary w-100">{{ 'login.submit'|trans }}</button>
				</form>

				<p class="text-body-secondary small mb-0 mt-4">Xivi {{ app_version }}</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</main>
{% endblock %}
